From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sean McCully <sean_mccully@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 13:39:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: NETSYS v3 feature port (RSS, HWLRO, PTP, reset)

Port the MediaTek SDK NETSYS v3 feature set to the mtk_eth_soc driver:
RSS and HWLRO receive paths with the extended 8-ring layout, hardware
timestamping (mtk_eth_ptp), the SDK FE reset/recovery state machine
(mtk_eth_reset), and the standalone SGMII helper.

Unlike the SDK original, no compile-time NETSYS_V* configuration is
introduced: all generation-dependent constants (register windows, ring
and IRQ counts, interrupt masks, reset bits, descriptor length
packing, SRAM offset) are selected at runtime via
mtk_is_netsys_v2/v3_or_greater() and the per-SoC data, so one kernel
image continues to serve all NETSYS generations as with the upstream
driver. TNL/TOPS tunnel offload, the vendor debugfs interface and the
netfilter extensions are intentionally not included. PPE roaming
activation remains disabled pending further integration.

The MT7988 device tree gains the extended clock set, named FE/PDMA
interrupts and syscon references in the mt7988a.dtsi NETSYS v3 patch;
missing clocks are only fatal when listed in the per-SoC
required_clks, so other NETSYS generations keep their existing device
trees. Runtime behaviour on NETSYS v1/v2 SoCs should still be
regression tested; the v1/v2 branches preserve the previous
constants.

Make the board's passive SFP/PHY mux transition transactional: stop and
disconnect the old endpoint under RTNL, route the SerDes lane before
creating the replacement phylink, and restore the original endpoint if
creation or reopen fails. A state bit separate from FE reset serializes
mux replacement without applying SER PHY semantics to the other MACs.

Build the PTP implementation only when it is reachable from mtk_eth and
provide no-PTP stubs for legacy subtargets whose Ethernet driver is built
in while the PTP core is modular. Compile and call the PPE debugfs support
only when CONFIG_DEBUG_FS is enabled. Keep required clock masks and their
lookups 64-bit so MT7987/MT7988 clock indices above bit 31 also compile on
32-bit MediaTek subtargets.

Signed-off-by: Sean McCully <sean_mccully@yahoo.com>
